type: software
title: "Система оценки качества ответов больших языковых моделей по новостным текстам стран Восточной Азии"
abstract: >-
  Bachelor's thesis repository (Faculty of Computational Mathematics and Cybernetics,
  Lomonosov Moscow State University): a system for evaluating the quality of large language
  model answers to questions about East Asian news texts in a cross-lingual setting (questions
  in Russian, sources in Chinese-language media). The object of measurement is the answer to a
  question about a frozen corpus snapshot, not the model. The system comprises a formal problem
  statement with a time-invariance predicate that restricts the golden set to static questions;
  a golden set of at least 150 questions (including questions whose correct answer is an
  abstention) with reference answers, aliases and supporting document identifiers, annotated
  independently by three annotators with Krippendorff's alpha of at least 0.67; a family of
  reference-based, citation, abstention and retrieval metrics including a language-model judge
  that is meta-evaluated separately for reliability and validity (Spearman correlation with
  human ratings of at least 0.5); and a statistical protocol (paired bootstrap, Wilcoxon
  signed-rank test with Holm correction, Cliff's delta) for comparing a production
  retrieval-augmented system with six open models with and without retrieval. The current corpus
  is Chinese-language media (PRC, Taiwan, Hong Kong, Singapore); extension to Japanese and Korean
  sources is future work.
